  abstract    = {Is geography destiny? This paper exploits a storm in 1825 that created a navigable waterway in northwestern Denmark as a natural experiment to estimate the causal effect of market access on long-run economic development. The estimated elasticity of geography-induced market access is 1.6, with lasting effects on population and economic activity.},
